  "localBiteReport": "As of mid-October 2026, the Destin Fishing Rodeo is underway and the inshore bite on Choctawhatchee Bay is heating up. Redfish and speckled trout are active in the bayous and on the flats, with slot reds being caught around docks and channel drop-offs. A local Santa Rosa Beach guide noted trout are still coming in alongside the reds, and expects sheepshead to pick up on structure in the bay in coming weeks. Flounder gigging was reported as starting to improve in early September and typically strengthens through October. Water temperature is 78°F. Note: the most recent Half Hitch Destin report available is from September 28 (about 3 weeks ago), and the captainexperiences.com guide reports are from approximately 1–2 weeks ago.",
